project Factorial
target console
runtime AgentRuntime 1.0

entry console main

type FactorialCounter I64
type FactorialAccumulator I64
type PositiveFactorialStep I64

error MainError
errorCase MainError ConsoleWriteFailed ConsoleWriteError
errorCase MainError FactorialUpperLimitTooLarge
errorCase MainError FactorialAccumulatorOverflowed FactorialOverflowError

capability consoleStdoutWriteCapability console.stdout write

operation main
input operation main console Console
output operation main Result ExitCode MainError
effect main write console.stdout
useCapability main consoleStdoutWriteCapability
memory main heap no
memoryStackLimit main 16KiB
async main no

purpose operation main "Compute the factorial of factorialUpperLimit and print the result as a single line"
invariant operation main "At factorialLoopHead, currentFactorialAccumulator equals factorial(currentFactorialCounter - 1)"
invariant operation main "factorialUpperLimit must be less than or equal to factorialOverflowSafeUpperLimit before the loop runs"
invariant operation main "factorialStepValue is strictly greater than zero"

label startMain

storage local immutable factorialLowerLimit FactorialCounter 1
storage local immutable factorialUpperLimit FactorialCounter 10
storage local immutable factorialOverflowSafeUpperLimit FactorialCounter 20
storage local immutable factorialStepValue PositiveFactorialStep 1
storage local immutable factorialAccumulatorInitial FactorialAccumulator 1

storage local mutable currentFactorialCounter FactorialCounter factorialLowerLimit
storage local mutable currentFactorialAccumulator FactorialAccumulator factorialAccumulatorInitial

# rationale: Confirm factorialUpperLimit stays inside the range where I64 factorial accumulation is provably safe.
# The largest factorialUpperLimit whose factorial fits in a signed 64-bit integer is twenty, so any request
# beyond that must be rejected with a typed MainError variant rather than silently overflowing.
call factorialUpperLimitSafetyCheckCall FactorialCounter.lessThanOrEqual
argument factorialUpperLimitSafetyCheckCall left FactorialCounter factorialUpperLimit
argument factorialUpperLimitSafetyCheckCall right FactorialCounter factorialOverflowSafeUpperLimit
run factorialUpperLimitSafetyCheckCall
bind value factorialUpperLimitIsOverflowSafe Bool factorialUpperLimitSafetyCheckCall

branch if condition factorialUpperLimitIsOverflowSafe target factorialLoopHead
branch else target factorialUpperLimitRejected

label factorialLoopHead

# rationale: Continue while currentFactorialCounter is less than or equal to factorialUpperLimit.
call factorialRangeCheckCall FactorialCounter.lessThanOrEqual
argument factorialRangeCheckCall left FactorialCounter currentFactorialCounter
argument factorialRangeCheckCall right FactorialCounter factorialUpperLimit
run factorialRangeCheckCall
bind value factorialShouldContinue Bool factorialRangeCheckCall

branch if condition factorialShouldContinue target factorialLoopBody
branch else target factorialFinished

label factorialLoopBody

# rationale: Multiply currentFactorialAccumulator by currentFactorialCounter using checked arithmetic.
# A successful multiplication binds the new accumulator value; an overflow takes the failure leg and
# surfaces a typed FactorialOverflowError through MainError.FactorialAccumulatorOverflowed.
call factorialAccumulatorMultiplyCall FactorialAccumulator.checkedMultiplyByCounter
argument factorialAccumulatorMultiplyCall accumulator FactorialAccumulator currentFactorialAccumulator
argument factorialAccumulatorMultiplyCall counter FactorialCounter currentFactorialCounter
run factorialAccumulatorMultiplyCall
bind ok nextFactorialAccumulator FactorialAccumulator factorialAccumulatorMultiplyCall
bind error factorialAccumulatorOverflowError FactorialOverflowError factorialAccumulatorMultiplyCall
branch error source factorialAccumulatorMultiplyCall target factorialAccumulatorOverflowed

set memory currentFactorialAccumulator nextFactorialAccumulator

# rationale: Advance the counter by exactly factorialStepValue; the typed PositiveFactorialStep guarantees forward progress.
call factorialCounterIncrementCall FactorialCounter.addPositiveStep
argument factorialCounterIncrementCall counter FactorialCounter currentFactorialCounter
argument factorialCounterIncrementCall step PositiveFactorialStep factorialStepValue
run factorialCounterIncrementCall
bind value nextFactorialCounter FactorialCounter factorialCounterIncrementCall

set memory currentFactorialCounter nextFactorialCounter
jump target factorialLoopHead

label factorialFinished

# rationale: Emit the final accumulator as a single line of standard output.
call writeFinalFactorialAccumulatorCall console.writeIntegerLine
argument writeFinalFactorialAccumulatorCall console Console console
argument writeFinalFactorialAccumulatorCall value FactorialAccumulator currentFactorialAccumulator
run writeFinalFactorialAccumulatorCall
ignore void source writeFinalFactorialAccumulatorCall
bind error writeFinalFactorialAccumulatorError ConsoleWriteError writeFinalFactorialAccumulatorCall
branch error source writeFinalFactorialAccumulatorCall target consoleWriteFailed

storage local immutable successfulExitCode ExitCode 0
return ok successfulExitCode

label factorialUpperLimitRejected
# failure: The configured factorialUpperLimit exceeds the I64 overflow-safe limit; reject before any multiplication runs.
makeError factorialUpperLimitRejectedFailure MainError.FactorialUpperLimitTooLarge
return error factorialUpperLimitRejectedFailure

label factorialAccumulatorOverflowed
# failure: The checked multiplication reported overflow; carry the raw FactorialOverflowError through the typed MainError.
makeError factorialAccumulatorOverflowFailure MainError.FactorialAccumulatorOverflowed factorialAccumulatorOverflowError
return error factorialAccumulatorOverflowFailure

label consoleWriteFailed
# failure: The console write failed after the factorial value was already computed; surface as MainError.ConsoleWriteFailed.
makeError consoleWriteFailure MainError.ConsoleWriteFailed writeFinalFactorialAccumulatorError
return error consoleWriteFailure
